## Testing Requirements:

### Database Tests:
```python
# Test spatial queries
def test_spatial_queries():
    area = create_test_area_with_geometry()
    metrics = get_metrics_within_bounds(area.bounds)
    assert len(metrics) > 0

# Test NASA API integration
def test_nasa_api_spatial():
    nasa_data = fetch_nasa_data_with_bounds(test_bounds)
    assert nasa_data.coordinates is not None
```

### Frontend Tests:
```javascript
// Test spatial interactions
describe('Area Selection', () => {
  test('should select area and update context', () => {
    const areaData = selectAreaOnMap(mockCoordinates);
    expect(areaData.bounds).toBeDefined();
  });
});
```

## Deployment Checklist:
- [ ] PostgreSQL + PostGIS installed
- [ ] Database migrations applied
- [ ] NASA API keys configured
- [ ] Spatial indexes created
- [ ] Seed data loaded
- [ ] React build completed
- [ ] Spatial queries tested

## Forbidden Practices:
- Building features without database foundation
- Non-spatial API endpoints
- Generic AI responses without geographic context
- Static maps without interaction
- Ignoring NASA data integration
- Skipping spatial testing

---

**Rule: Always build spatial-first, test spatial functionality, deploy with spatial awareness!**